; DOMAIN: modular-parametrization [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-25]
; Claim: For an elliptic curve E over Q of conductor N, the Modularity Theorem yields a nonconstant morphism phi: X_0(N) -> E defined over Q, the modular parametrization, sending the cusp infinity to O. It arises from the weight-2 newform f of level N via the Eichler-Shimura construction: the differential phi^*(omega_E) = c * 2*pi*i*f(tau)*dtau (c the Manin constant), so pullback of the invariant differential is the modular form. The degree of phi is the modular degree deg(phi), a key arithmetic invariant bounding the congruence number and appearing in the BSD / Sha bounds. Composition with the uniformization H/Gamma_0(N) realizes E(C)=C/Lambda via the elliptic integral of f; Heegner points are images phi(x) of CM points x on X_0(N), feeding Gross-Zagier and the rank-1 BSD case. Bridge: genesis_shimura_taniyama (modularity provides the surjection X_0(N)->E from the newform f of level N=conductor) + genesis_frobenius_trace (phi^*omega = f dq/q so a_p(f)=a_p(E) match Fourier coeffs to point-count trace) + genesis_elliptic_curve (target E, phi(infinity)=O, pullback of invariant differential omega_E).
(= (modular-parametrization $E) (morphism (X0 (conductor $E)) $E (sends cusp-infinity O)))
(= (pullback-differential $E) (equal (pullback (modular-param $E) (invariant-diff $E)) (times (manin-constant $E) (newform-differential (newform $E)))))
(= (modular-degree $E) (degree (modular-parametrization $E)))
(= (uniformization $E) (via (upper-half-plane-mod Gamma0 (conductor $E)) (elliptic-integral (newform $E))))
(= (heegner-point $E $x) (image (modular-parametrization $E) (cm-point $x (X0 (conductor $E)))))